    "result_text": "The change is complete and green. Here's what I implemented and why it's placed where it is:\n\n## Summary\n\n`riskFlag` is a **derived, read-only response field** \u2014 it's computed from state already produced elsewhere in the owner pipeline, so it belongs in the response mapper alongside the other derived fields (`ownerSegment`, `identityKey`, `contactPreference`, \u2026), not as a new pipeline step.\n\n**Three edits, each in its natural home:**\n\n1. **`OwnerEmail.java`** \u2014 added `isDisposableAdjacent(email)`. The existing class already owns the disposable-domain blocklist and the \"what is this email's domain\" logic, so the \"adjacent\" notion belongs right next to `isDisposable`. I also extracted a private `domainOf(email)` helper and reused it from `isDisposable` (removing the duplicated `@`-parsing). \"Disposable-adjacent\" is defined cleanly as: the domain carries a known throwaway-mail service label (`mailinator`, `tempmail`, `guerrillamail`) as one of its dot-separated labels \u2014 catching subdomains (`x.mailinator.com`) and same-service-different-suffix (`mailinator.net`) that slip past the exact-match blocklist (exact matches are rejected at creation, so only adjacent ones can reach a stored owner).\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a small `riskFlag(owner)` default method that ORs the three conditions, and wired it via `@Mapping(... expression ...)`. It reuses existing entity state:\n   - *possible duplicate* \u2192 `owner.getPossibleDuplicate()`\n   - *disposable-adjacent email* \u2192 `OwnerEmail.isDisposableAdjacent(...)`\n   - *city over soft capacity* \u2192 `owner.getCapacityWarning()` (the soft-capacity band 40\u201349, already computed at creation)\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `riskFlag` read-only boolean to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n**Tests:** full suite green \u2014 `Tests run: 7, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, `BUILD SUCCESS`. The new `coreRiskFlagFalseNormally` passes (a fully-unique owner with no email, unique city, no duplicate \u2192 `false`).",
